        {
          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "Keccak-256 (Ethereum's pre-FIPS-202 Keccak variant, 0x01 padding — not standard SHA3-256) is eth-utils' only crypto primitive, consumed through eth_hash.auto with the backend chosen at import time (pycryptodome in dev/test per setup.py:13 and tox.ini:37). It powers three protocol-mandated operations: EIP-55 checksum addresses, 4-byte ABI function selectors, and 32-byte event log topics. Reachability note: the algorithm is fixed by the Ethereum protocol specification (EIP-55, ABI selector rules) "
        },
